The URL has stray quote characters from how xargs exported it. Check what's actually in it:

```bash
echo "[$DATABASE_URL]"
```

Then re-export cleanly without xargs:

```bash
export DATABASE_URL=$(grep '^DATABASE_URL=' ~/Musaddique/Smart\ Renewal\ Advisor/.env | cut -d'=' -f2- | tr -d '"' | tr -d "'")
```

Then try again:

```bash
PGURL=$(echo $DATABASE_URL | sed 's/?sslmode=require//')
PGSSLMODE=require psql "$PGURL" -c "\dn"
```
